---
description: Security rules for Solidity smart contracts (access control, reentrancy, external calls, oracles, signatures, upgradeability)
globs: **/*.sol
alwaysApply: false
---

When writing or reviewing Solidity, follow the `solidity-security` skill: pin the compiler (>= 0.8), check
the caller on every privileged function (never `tx.origin`), update state before external calls and guard
them against reentrancy, check every low-level call and use SafeERC20, never `delegatecall` caller-supplied
addresses, don't derive randomness from block values or prices from AMM reserves, use EIP-712 signatures with
nonces and deadlines, protect initializers. Before a deploy, run the Chain Preflight scan
(`chain-preflight scan . --report`). Static analysis is not an audit.
